# crontab.example - weekly automatic run of the GSE66494 pipeline.
#
# Install:  crontab -e   then paste the last line below and save.
# Check:    crontab -l
# Fields:   minute hour day-of-month month day-of-week command
#
# This line runs every Monday at 03:00. It goes to the project folder
# (here ~/projet_maladie: change it if your repo is elsewhere), activates the
# Python venv, runs run.sh, and appends the output to logs/cron.log.
# run.sh also writes its own timestamped log in logs/ and a dated archive in
# results/archives/ at every run.
0 3 * * 1 cd "$HOME/projet_maladie" && . .venv/bin/activate && ./run.sh >> logs/cron.log 2>&1
